WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:27.480
Any condition or disease that damages
your heart's ability to pump blood can cause heart failure.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.220
For example, the most common cause is coronary artery disease,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.620
in which blood vessels that supply your
heart muscle, called coronary arteries,

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.920
become blocked by a fatty substance called plaque.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.280
Other common causes of heart failure
include:

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.400
uncontrolled high blood pressure,

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.500
and high blood sugar in diabetes.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.220
Less common causes of heart failure include:

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:57.400
diseased, infected, or damaged heart valves,

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.200
irregular heartbeats called arrhythmias,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.440
heart defects,

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.080
poisons or substance abuse,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.200
lung diseases,

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.980
and breathing problems during sleep called sleep apnea.

